    "show_share": true,
    "description": "It is estimated that of the 130 million infants born each year worldwide, 4 million die in the first 28 days of life. Two-thirds of the world's neonatal deaths occur in just 10 countries, mostly in Asia. Pakistan is number three among these countries. 298,000 neonatal deaths occur every year at a rate of 49 per 1000 live births, with Pakistan accounting for 7% of global neonatal deaths overall [1] . These are shocking statistics.",
